a stand-in declaring a library its genuine stanza lacks is refused, naming both stanzas (the gh-ocannl-2234 shape): true
a genuine stanza declaring more than its stand-in, by public names and preprocessors, is accepted: true
a library the genuine stanza names only in a select condition counts as declared: true
a library only a sibling alternative of the arm's own select names is refused: true
a stand-in re-export the genuine stanza does not make is refused: true
a package stand-in whose package the genuine stanza never names is refused: true
a library an availability-only exception names is excused: true
an availability-only exception that excuses nothing is refused: true
a stand-in depending on another library of the stand-in tree is refused: true
a stand-in copy of a file no stanza compiles is refused: true
a stand-in preprocessor its genuine stanza does not run is refused: true
a preprocessing form the scan does not read is refused: true
a vendor arm copied and compiled under the stand-ins is accepted, its fallback undemanded: true
a vendor arm copied by a copy_files glob is accepted: true
a default-module stand-in library beside a copy_files glob is refused: true
an arm gated on no vendor library is not demanded: true
an arm that only forbids a vendor library is not demanded: true
a vendor arm nothing copies is refused, naming its dune file: true
an arm gated on a vendor backend's public name alone is demanded: true
a copy of a same-named file from another directory does not count: true
a copy outside arrayjit/vendor_stubs does not count: true
a copied arm no library compiles is refused: true
a tree with no package stand-in is refused: true
a tree with no backend stand-in is refused: true
a dune file that does not read is refused: true
an empty dune-file corpus is refused: true

